2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,35,27626,594,4540,1372,11,400,18,18,21,3,481,400,22,21,17,19,4779,702,279,3343,429,279,2326,48342,9252,11,400,18,18,21,4779,16819,279,1985,315,279,1537,3040,18509,11,400,22,1124,15136,220,21,1124,15136,220,17,1124,15136,220,19,2418,2585,1657,8094,48342,4540,5109,7167,448,400,18,18,21,3,614,419,3343,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nDerek's phone number, $336$ - $7624,$ has the property that the three-digit prefix, $336,$ equals the product of the last four digits, $7 \\times 6 \\times 2 \\times 4.$ How many seven-digit phone numbers beginning with $336$ have this property?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9a86c75e35504019e0b32d64e9a9575ba110e98bbc50fb8825fdf1b7bb5ce40a"},"seconds":48.690061807632446,"seed":1125129982539689323,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to find how many seven-digit phone numbers of the form \\(336-ABCD\\) have the property that the three-digit prefix \\(336\\) equals the product of the last four digits \\(A \\times B \\times C \\times D\\).\n\nFirst, let's understand the condition:\n\\[336 = A \\times B \\times C \\times D\\]\n\nWe need to find all combinations of \\(A, B, C,\\) and \\(D\\) (each being a digit from 0 to 9) such that their product equals 336.\n\n### Step 1: Factorize 336\nTo simplify the problem, we start by factorizing 336:\n\\[336 = 2^4 \\times 3 \\times 7\\]\n\n### Step 2: Find Valid Combinations\nWe need to distribute these factors among four digits \\(A, B, C,\\) and \\(D\\) such that each digit is between 0 and 9.\n\n#### Possible Distributions:\n1. \\(A = 7, B = 6, C = 4, D = 2\\)\n   \\[7 \\times 6 \\times 4 \\times 2 = 336\\]\n   This is a valid combination.\n\n2. Other combinations:\n   - We need to check other distributions of the factors \\(2^4, 3, 7\\) among four digits. For instance:\n     - \\(A = 8, B = 6, C = 7, D = 1\\)\n     - \\(A = 8, B = 7, C = 6, D = 1\\)\n     - \\(A = 7, B = 8, C = 6, D = 1\\)\n     - \\(A = 7, B = 6, C = 8, D = 1\\)\n     - \\(A = 6, B = 7, C = 8, D = 1\\)\n     - \\(A = 6, B = 8, C = 7, D = 1\\)\n     - \\(A = 1, B = 7, C = 8, D = 6\\)\n     - \\(A = 1, B = 8, C = 7, D = 6\\)\n     - \\(A = 1, B = 6, C = 8, D = 7\\)\n     - \\(A = 1, B = 6, C = 7, D = 8\\)\n     - \\(A = 1, B = 8, C = 6, D = 7\\)\n     - \\(A = 1, B = 7, C = 6, D = 8\\)\n     - And so on...\n\n### Step 3: Count Valid Combinations\nWe need to count all unique permutations of the above valid combinations. For example, the combination \\(7, 6, 4, 2\\) can be permuted in \\(4! = 24\\) ways.\n\n### Step 4: Verify and Count\nWe verify that all combinations are valid and count them. For example:\n- \\(7, 6, 4, 2\\) can be permuted in \\(24\\) ways.\n- \\(8, 6, 7, 1\\) can be permuted in \\(24\\) ways.\n- And so on...\n\n### Conclusion\nAfter verifying and counting all unique permutations, we find that there are 24 valid combinations for each set of digits.\n\nThus, the total number of valid seven-digit phone numbers is:\n\\[\\boxed{24}\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{24}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
